1. Clone the repository
```bash
   git clone https://github.com/your-username/your-repo-name.git
   cd your-repo-name
```
2. Install dependencies
```bash
   pip install pandas numpy
```
3. Run the script
```bash
   python data_clean.py
```

The cleaned dataset will be saved as `Cleaned_indian_employee_data.csv` in the same directory.

## 📊 Cleaning Steps Applied

| Step | Description |
|------|-------------|
| 1 | Load raw CSV data |
| 2 | Check and report missing values |
| 3 | Impute missing Salary (mean) and Performance Rating (median) |
| 4 | Replace infinite values with NaN |
| 5 | Fill remaining missing numeric values |
| 6 | Remove duplicate rows |
| 7 | Fix negative salary entries |
| 8 | Remove statistical outliers (3σ rule) |
| 9 | Export cleaned data to CSV |

